{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972882-has-anyone-done-a-chronicle-with-the-technocracy-and-traditions-reversed-in-power","id":972882,"title":"Has anyone done a chronicle with the Technocracy and Traditions reversed in power?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T19:17:15-07:00","id":972882,"title":"Has anyone done a chronicle with the Technocracy and Traditions reversed in power?","content":"Let's say the Traditions dominated until today and the Technocracy are now the downtrodden outcasts, trying desperately to bring order and sanity to a world gone mad(in their eyes). Dragons flitting about, people communicating by crystal balls small enough to fit on your wrist(can also tell time and lucky numbers), spirits being used as rickshaw drivers, and people discussing current events like the recent landmark United States Supreme Mystics decision regarding the rights of partial human species(like werewolves). While I'm envisioning a world almost identical to our own but with magical counterparts to technology, I'm wondering if anyone has done one with any variation on that theme(divergent histories, altered chronologies like certain events happened sooner/later, etc...). If so, how did it work out?<br /> <br /> Edit - And I was looking for an option to delete this post but I'm not seeing one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3716,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","user":"Mrtwist","date":". 09-19-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:25:45-07:00","id":972884,"title":"","content":"No, primarily because the Traditions do not have a unified paradigm that would lead to the contemporary world. I think that the Earth would be much less advanced and much less populated because the Traditions are not interested in progress. Instead, you would have the classic fantasy world, though the vampires and werewolves would be more challenging. The average suffering of mundane humans would be greater because they would lack modern medicine. Women would be effectively be reproductive slaves, just like they were when the world was Traditional, and women and children would be gang raped by ever passing army, just like they were when the world was more Traditional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:13:56-07:00","id":972899,"title":"","content":"It was called the Dark Ages. and instead of the Technocrats They were the Order of Reason. Valiant fighters for the Common Man against the Oppressive crafty witches, the Mad Wizards, the Tyrannical Church, and the Satanic Pagans in the woods","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":". 09-19-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:48:32-07:00","id":972965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972882-has-anyone-done-a-chronicle-with-the-technocracy-and-traditions-reversed-in-power?p=972884#post972884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, primarily because the Traditions do not have a unified paradigm that would lead to the contemporary world. I think that the Earth would be much less advanced and much less populated because the Traditions are not interested in progress. Instead, you would have the classic fantasy world, though the vampires and werewolves would be more challenging. The average suffering of mundane humans would be greater because they would lack modern medicine. Women would be effectively be reproductive slaves, just like they were when the world was Traditional, and women and children would be gang raped by ever passing army, just like they were when the world was more Traditional.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You surely mention sex a lot.<br /> <br /> Well, on topic.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it depends what year Traditions began to dominate. Was it since Dark Ages? Was it after Reinnassance? When Sons of Ether, or Virtual Adepts joined?<br /> <br /> If since Dark Ages.. honestly it's hard to imagine where we would be. Electrodyne Engineers and Order of Hermes always pushed to progress, but their own kind of progress if that tells you about anything.<br /> <br /> If since Reinnassance, I'd imagine spiritualism and technopagans being extremelly popular nowadays.<br /> <br /> If since the rebellion from Society of Ether or Virtual Adepts, the world would be similar to what we have right now - in fact, I'd even say Science could skyrocket to amazing achievements, but you know, I'd take inspiration from Warhammer universe on that - the mankind faces the Things That Man Was Not Meant To Know, and in endless conquest, the Milky Way galaxy would be red from all the blood (though this whole galaxy thing would happen about 100-200 years later or so if Tradition dominance was established after Society of Ether and Virtual Adepts joined, and with less Space Marines dudes or other weirdos. Just the whole theme about cruel future in endless conquest).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:54:25-07:00","id":972967,"title":"","content":"I am in the progress of possibly creating a world dominated by mystics.<br /> Currently we have just started in 1450. All players except one are unaging, and depending on their actions the history will be different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:26:03-07:00","id":973057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrtwist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972882-has-anyone-done-a-chronicle-with-the-technocracy-and-traditions-reversed-in-power#post972882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say the Traditions dominated until today and the Technocracy are now the downtrodden outcasts, trying desperately to bring order and sanity to a world gone mad(in their eyes). Dragons flitting about, people communicating by crystal balls small enough to fit on your wrist(can also tell time and lucky numbers), spirits being used as rickshaw drivers, and people discussing current events like the recent landmark United States Supreme Mystics decision regarding the rights of partial human species(like werewolves). While I'm envisioning a world almost identical to our own but with magical counterparts to technology, I'm wondering if anyone has done one with any variation on that theme(divergent histories, altered chronologies like certain events happened sooner/later, etc...). If so, how did it work out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the biggest issue is that the only reason the Traditions were even willing to work together is a shared threat. While it is entirely plausible for a Mystical alliance to rise up to control the world, it would not be the Nine. The actual mix would depend a great deal on what their goals and ideals, but some good candidates would be The Order of Hermes (who discovered Consensual Reality), the Cabal of Pure Thought or some other faction of Christian mystics, the Taftani, the Chakravanti, the Wu Lung (if they were promised complete dominion over China), and anyone else who had enough influence over their local consensus that letting them join was easier than stamping them out.<br /> <br /> Also of note, their rivals would not be 100% scientific. Instead, anyone pushed to the edges, especially those who opposed the aforementioned goals and ideals, would make up the resistance. If the Mystical Hegemony was based around keeping Magic in the hands of an Enlightened elite, expect a strong populist theme in their enemies. If they are based around a proper order to the heavens, expect a anarchistic streak.<br /> <br /> And if there is a strong scientific presence in the resistance, expect to see the students of the <i>Kitab-al-Alacir</i>. The Etherites always find a way of getting involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:52:31-07:00","id":973107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrtwist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972882-has-anyone-done-a-chronicle-with-the-technocracy-and-traditions-reversed-in-power#post972882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone done a chronicle with the Technocracy and Traditions reversed in power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not, But I had one in program.<br /> It was in my End of Times crossover chronicle, with the impending Gehenna/Apocalypse/Great-Whatever. After vampires and werewolves do their things and the wolrd is confronted with their existence, the Consensus begin to crumble, thus the common ( &quot;technocrat&quot; ) technology begin to fail.<br /> Then the mystic arts shine again, and then things get ugly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:35:03-07:00","id":973222,"title":"","content":"I agree with the others who have written about how a Traditions-run world would look, as in it depends on who and at what particular time period things solidified. However, a &quot; rebel Technocracy on the fringes&quot; certainly wouldn't look like what you seem to be thinking.<br /> <br /> You have to remember that science and technology as we know it is a Technocratic construction, effectively propaganda, and pretty much how their magick is performed. Again, in Mage, &quot;science&quot; and &quot;technology&quot; are just codified and easily accessible forms of &quot;magic.&quot; It also is the product of years of R&amp;D into what can effectively be introduced into the general Consensus as repeatable and reliable by the Masses. It's not really research into how things works, but research into what people are willing to believe, or how that belief can be directed and limited. Let's take it back down to what they originally were and represented during the early days of the Order of Reason: spreading the wealth of power around to those who can't inherently wield it, general safety to the Masses. Even early Order of Reason &quot;tech&quot; that was pushed was mildly magickal. Remember, religion had a pretty central role in those times, even for the Order.<br /> <br /> What would this look like in a &quot;Tradition-controlled&quot; world? Moving past the arguments of what exactly that world would look like, let's just operate on the assumption that there is still some manner of concentration of power to the magickal elites and very little trickle-down to the Sleepers. There might be some manner of society built around mundane &quot;magic,&quot; likely parallel to the ubiquitous sort of magic available to even non-magical people in the world of Harry Potter (squibs, or whatever they're called).<br /> <br /> So, to me, an organization that could possibly arise in a Traditional world with the goals of the Technocracy would probably end up looking a lot like the early Order of Reason, but maybe a bit more magical. If magic is a sort of ubiquitous thing and the only difference is the access to it, I'd imagine some kind of socialist revolution involving leaking of rituals and mass-produced artifacts. Complex magicks would be distilled down to easily understood steps and spread around. If the concept of the Consensus has been discovered as is being used by our little rogue Order, then it's really just a case of demonstrating enough times the efficacy of the magics, the technology of the setting, and spreading belief.<br /> <br /> Finally, I want to push back against this meme of &quot;everything was shitty hundreds of years ago because the Traditions were in charge.&quot; Progress was being made in regular, human society, with our without supernatural interference. There may have been areas of abuse by Awakened individuals, but for the most part they cloistered together and didn't interact with those &quot;below&quot; them. The world wasn't being held down by any sort of Traditional chokehold for the sake of their own power, and the concept of the Consensus was just barely coming around by the time the Order blew it all up and put us on the path. Would we have ended up in a Traditional world with &quot;magical&quot; technology? Maybe. But this idea that the shittiness of the dark ages lies wholly at the feet of the proto-Traditions is <i>canonically</i> wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:15:30-07:00","id":973248,"title":"","content":"If you read Dark Ages: Mage, you probably have the best starting point. There's no centralized opposition to mystic mages, but the organizations that eventually formed the Order of Reason largely still exist. Claudius Dediticius already wrote his <i>Revelation of the Pure Thought of God</i> and formed the Gabrielites. The scattered Cosians after the fall of Rome are still out there. The Artificers and Craftmasons have lots of small lodges, some of whom are probably in touch with the Order of Hermes. <br /> <br /> In other words, you have a heterodox world based on localized power. Do the Old Faith (never having been forged into the Verbena by Gabrielite depredations) still concentrate in English/Gaulish lands? Do the Valdaermen still join with a greater group to avoid extinction as Christianity spreads northward?<br /> <br /> Without scientific thought spurring the Enlightenment, the real question is whether some other labor-saving technique shows up. In the real world, getting more done with fewer people raises standards of living and allows a rich middle class to challenge the nobility for power. Magick can do the same, but is anyone going to spread it out to Sleepers? I doubt it - none of the magickal groups have that as a driving goal. So power remains in central hands, uprisings are limited and easily crushed, and the world is highly stratified. Different geographic areas are dominated by different magickal groups and flavor the culture there. Some groups die out and others sprout up as they compete to become the dominant paradigm, but without consolidation, the world is a patchwork of different Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> If you want something that resembles our world a little more, invent a group that uses mystic magick but wants to spread it to everyone - perhaps another Hermetic offshoot. Then you can see the same societal change - just instead of early factories and smokestacks, you have rows of bound spirits or persistent effects working in tandem to produce a consumer product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:29:18-08:00","id":1006397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972882-has-anyone-done-a-chronicle-with-the-technocracy-and-traditions-reversed-in-power?p=973248#post973248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want something that resembles our world a little more, invent a group that uses mystic magick but wants to spread it to everyone - perhaps another Hermetic offshoot. Then you can see the same societal change - just instead of early factories and smokestacks, you have rows of bound spirits or persistent effects working in tandem to produce a consumer product.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i><u>This.</u></i></b><br /> <br /> I could see the Solificati filling this role, especially if the Celestial Chorus joined them. No one is gonna be too upset by stronger metals for their plows, nails, swords, armor, hammers, etc. Get the Church to give it the stamp of approval and you're good to go. Heck, I could see some would-be Artificers, Cosians, and Craftmasons getting in on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:01:07-08:00","id":1010123,"title":"","content":"well, I think that if properly thought out the mystics dominated world wouldn't resemble modern one at all. Though I agree that it greatly depends on the process of divergence, mystic dominated world would still see advancement both magical and technological. Population would be vastly smaller, not necessarily because of lower living standards, but because mystic mages would be against uncontrolled population booms and destruction of wild/sacred places. There would definitely be much more mythical creatures, spirits, Fae and werecretures, with humanity mixing with them much more frequently. On the other hand a lot of infrastructure would be substituted by the sorcerers, lesser magic and weaker supernaturals. Plus, if mages increase in power there well could be large scale wars with other supernaturals, over quintessence or simply because they don't like you, and larger changes with umbra s gountlet will be weaker and mages may well expand their influence on the other side. I would also expect more liberalism, as mages tend to use drugs, gender-change, etc. As for the dominant paradigms:<br /> Europe: Hermetics/Celestial Chorus or Verbena<br /> Middle East: Taftani or Subtle Ones<br /> Oceania and arctic: Dreamspeakers<br /> China: Wu Lung<br /> Japan and Himalaya: Dreamspeakers/Akashiana<br /> India: Chakravanti and Sahajaia<br /> <br /> And of course, above it all a cosmic game of chess between the Hidden Masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}